stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    accTitle: What happens to the copy of a document
    accDescr: An exported document is in the archive. Moved to the trash in Paperless, or gone from Paperless without the trash for N complete scans, its copy moves to _Deleted; restored in Paperless, it moves back to the archive. Deleted for good in Paperless, the copy in _Deleted is deleted in Nextcloud after N complete scans, when permanent deletion is on. A copy in the archive whose document is gone from Paperless without the trash for N complete scans is deleted directly when permanent and direct deletion are on.
    state "In the archive" as archive
    state "In _Deleted" as deleted
    state "Deleted in Nextcloud" as gone
    [*] --> archive: exported
    archive --> deleted: moved to the trash<br>in Paperless, or gone<br>without the trash<br>for N complete scans
    deleted --> archive: restored<br>in Paperless
    deleted --> gone: deleted for good<br>in Paperless, after<br>N complete scans, with<br>permanent deletion on
    archive --> gone: gone without the trash<br>for N complete scans,<br>with permanent and<br>direct deletion on
